IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part7-pari-mutuel.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, section 204 (Exemption: pari-mutuel betting on horse-races).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- The rates, percentages and numbers of races the text leaves to the regulations or to the Governor in Council are INPUTS here, never a number from memory.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- The core `Party` has no "association", "officer appointed by the Minister" or "Receiver General", so this module declares its own party type (NEEDS-CORE.md).

§ `Section 204 -- Exemption`

DECLARE `s 204 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 204 a person or association`
    `s 204 an association operating a pari-mutuel system`

DECLARE `s 204 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 204(3) use a pari-mutuel system of betting in respect of a horse-race`
    `s 204(4) pay to the Receiver General the fraction of the total amount bet` HAS `s 204(4) the amount paid, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 204(5) deduct or retain an amount from the total amount of money, bets or stakes`

-- src:4227 | (a) any person or association by reason of his or their becoming the custodian or depository of any money, property or valuable thing staked, to be paid to
-- src:4228 | (i) the winner of a lawful race, sport, game or exercise,
-- src:4229 | (ii) the owner of a horse engaged in a lawful race, or
-- src:4230 | (iii) the winner of any bets between not more than ten individuals;
@ref s 204(1)(a) (src:4227-4230)
GIVEN `the person or association becomes the custodian or depository of money, property or valuable thing staked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be paid to the winner of a lawful race, sport, game or exercise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be paid to the owner of a horse engaged in a lawful race` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be paid to the winner of bets between individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of individuals between whom the bets are` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1)(a) sections 201 and 202 do not apply to the custodian or depository` MEANS
    IF     `the person or association becomes the custodian or depository of money, property or valuable thing staked`
       AND (   `it is to be paid to the winner of a lawful race, sport, game or exercise`
            OR `it is to be paid to the owner of a horse engaged in a lawful race`
            OR (`it is to be paid to the winner of bets between individuals` AND `the number of individuals between whom the bets are` AT MOST 10))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply to (a) any person or association by reason of his or their becoming the custodian or depository of any money, property or valuable thing staked, to be paid to"

-- src:4231 | (b) a private bet between individuals not engaged in any way in the business of betting;
@ref s 204(1)(b) (src:4231-4231)
GIVEN `the bet is a private bet between individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individuals are engaged in any way in the business of betting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1)(b) sections 201 and 202 do not apply to the private bet` MEANS
    IF `the bet is a private bet between individuals` AND (NOT `the individuals are engaged in any way in the business of betting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply to ... a private bet between individuals not engaged in any way in the business of betting"

-- src:4232 | (c) bets made or records of bets made through the agency of a pari-mutuel system on running, trotting or pacing horse-races if
-- src:4233 | (i) the bets or records of bets are made on the race-course of an association in respect of races conducted at that race-course or another race-course in or out of Canada, and, in the case of a race conducted on a race-course situated outside Canada, the governing body that regulates the race has been certified as acceptable by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food or a person designated by that Minister pursuant to subsection (8.1) and that Minister or person has permitted pari-mutuel betting in Canada on the race pursuant to that subsection, and
-- src:4234 | (ii) the provisions of this section and the regulations are complied with.
@ref s 204(1)(c) (src:4232-4234)
GIVEN `the bets or records of bets are made through the agency of a pari-mutuel system on running, trotting or pacing horse-races` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are made on the race-course of an association in respect of races conducted at that race-course or another race-course in or out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are deemed to be made on the race-course of the association, by s 204(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the race is conducted on a race-course situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the governing body that regulates the race has been certified as acceptable by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food or a person designated by that Minister pursuant to subsection (8.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that Minister or person has permitted pari-mutuel betting in Canada on the race pursuant to that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of this section and the regulations are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1)(c) sections 201 and 202 do not apply to the pari-mutuel bets` MEANS
    IF     `the bets or records of bets are made through the agency of a pari-mutuel system on running, trotting or pacing horse-races`
       AND (   `they are made on the race-course of an association in respect of races conducted at that race-course or another race-course in or out of Canada`
            OR `they are deemed to be made on the race-course of the association, by s 204(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (   (NOT `the race is conducted on a race-course situated outside Canada`)
            OR (    `the governing body that regulates the race has been certified as acceptable by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food or a person designated by that Minister pursuant to subsection (8.1)`
                AND `that Minister or person has permitted pari-mutuel betting in Canada on the race pursuant to that subsection`))
       AND `the provisions of this section and the regulations are complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply to ... bets made or records of bets made through the agency of a pari-mutuel system on running, trotting or pacing horse-races if"

-- src:4226 | 204 (1) Sections 201 and 202 do not apply to
@ref s 204(1) (src:4226-4226)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) applies, by s 204(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) applies, by s 204(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c) applies, by s 204(1)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1) sections 201 and 202 do not apply` MEANS
    IF     `paragraph (a) applies, by s 204(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `paragraph (b) applies, by s 204(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `paragraph (c) applies, by s 204(1)(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): sections 201 and 202 "do not apply to" the three listed cases; for any other case the text is silent

-- src:4236 | (1.1) For greater certainty, a person may, in accordance with the regulations, do anything described in section 201 or 202, if the person does it for the purposes of legal pari-mutuel betting.
@ref s 204(1.1) (src:4236-4236)
GIVEN `the person does it in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does it for the purposes of legal pari-mutuel betting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1.1) the person may do anything described in section 201 or 202` MEANS
    IF `the person does it in accordance with the regulations` AND `the person does it for the purposes of legal pari-mutuel betting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person may, in accordance with the regulations, do anything described in section 201 or 202, if the person does it for the purposes of legal pari-mutuel betting" (a grant: the text says nothing of the case outside it)

-- src:4238 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), bets made, in accordance with the regulations, in a betting theatre referred to in paragraph (8)(e), or by any means of telecommunication to the race-course of an association or to such a betting theatre, are deemed to be made on the race-course of the association.
@ref s 204(2) (src:4238-4238)
GIVEN `the bets are made in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are made in a betting theatre referred to in paragraph (8)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are made by means of telecommunication to the race-course of an association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are made by means of telecommunication to such a betting theatre` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(2) the bets are deemed to be made on the race-course of the association` MEANS
    IF     `the bets are made in accordance with the regulations`
       AND (   `they are made in a betting theatre referred to in paragraph (8)(e)`
            OR `they are made by means of telecommunication to the race-course of an association`
            OR `they are made by means of telecommunication to such a betting theatre`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "bets made, in accordance with the regulations, in a betting theatre ... or by any means of telecommunication to the race-course of an association or to such a betting theatre, are deemed to be made on the race-course" (for the purposes of paragraph (1)(c))

-- src:4240 | (3) No person or association shall use a pari-mutuel system of betting in respect of a horse-race unless the system has been approved by and its operation is carried on under the supervision of an officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food.
@ref s 204(3) (src:4240-4240)
GIVEN `the system has been approved by an officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food, and its operation is carried on under the supervision of such an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(3) the person or association is prohibited from using the pari-mutuel system` MEANS
    IF `the system has been approved by an officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food, and its operation is carried on under the supervision of such an officer`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person or association shall use a pari-mutuel system of betting in respect of a horse-race unless the system has been approved by and its operation is carried on under the supervision of an officer" (the prohibition is lifted on that condition: marginal reading M2)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 204(3) (src:4240-4240)
GIVEN `the system has been approved by an officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food, and its operation is carried on under the supervision of such an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 204 party` `s 204 act`
`s 204(3) the duty not to use a pari-mutuel system` MEANS
    IF `the system has been approved by an officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food, and its operation is carried on under the supervision of such an officer`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `s 204 a person or association`
         SHANT `s 204(3) use a pari-mutuel system of betting in respect of a horse-race`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 204 a person or association` BECAUSE "s 204(3): a pari-mutuel system was used that had not been approved and supervised"

-- src:4242 | (4) Every person or association operating a pari-mutuel system of betting in accordance with this section in respect of a horse-race, whether or not the person or association is conducting the race-meeting at which the race is run, shall pay to the Receiver General in respect of each individual pool of the race and each individual feature pool one-half of one per cent, or such greater fraction not exceeding one per cent as may be fixed by the Governor in Council, of the total amount of money that is bet through the agency of the pari-mutuel system of betting.
@ref s 204(4) (src:4242-4242)
GIVEN `the total amount of money that is bet through the agency of the pari-mutuel system, for the pool, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the greater fraction fixed by the Governor in Council, as a decimal (0 if none is fixed)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 204(4) the amount to be paid to the Receiver General for the pool` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the greater fraction fixed by the Governor in Council, as a decimal (0 if none is fixed)` EQUALS 0
        THEN JUST (`the total amount of money that is bet through the agency of the pari-mutuel system, for the pool, in dollars` TIMES 0.005)   -- "one-half of one per cent"
        IF `the greater fraction fixed by the Governor in Council, as a decimal (0 if none is fixed)` GREATER THAN 0.005 AND `the greater fraction fixed by the Governor in Council, as a decimal (0 if none is fixed)` AT MOST 0.01
        THEN JUST (`the total amount of money that is bet through the agency of the pari-mutuel system, for the pool, in dollars` TIMES `the greater fraction fixed by the Governor in Council, as a decimal (0 if none is fixed)`)   -- "such greater fraction not exceeding one per cent as may be fixed by the Governor in Council"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a fraction that is not greater than one-half of one per cent, or exceeds one per cent, is not a fraction this subsection lets the Governor in Council fix

@ref s 204(4) (src:4242-4242)
GIVEN `the amount to be paid to the Receiver General for the pool` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 204 party` `s 204 act`
`s 204(4) the duty to pay the Receiver General` MEANS
    PARTY `s 204 an association operating a pari-mutuel system`
    MUST `s 204(4) pay to the Receiver General the fraction of the total amount bet` paid PROVIDED paid EQUALS `the amount to be paid to the Receiver General for the pool`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 204 an association operating a pari-mutuel system` BECAUSE "s 204(4): the fraction of the total amount bet was not paid to the Receiver General"

-- src:4244 | (5) Where any person or association becomes a custodian or depository of any money, bet or stakes under a pari-mutuel system in respect of a horse-race, that person or association shall not deduct or retain any amount from the total amount of money, bets or stakes unless it does so pursuant to subsection (6).
@ref s 204(5) (src:4244-4244)
GIVEN `the deduction or retention is made pursuant to subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(5) the person or association is prohibited from deducting or retaining an amount` MEANS
    IF `the deduction or retention is made pursuant to subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not deduct or retain any amount from the total amount of money, bets or stakes unless it does so pursuant to subsection (6)" (the prohibition is lifted on that condition: marginal reading M2)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 204(5) (src:4244-4244)
GIVEN `the deduction or retention is made pursuant to subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 204 party` `s 204 act`
`s 204(5) the duty not to deduct or retain` MEANS
    IF `the deduction or retention is made pursuant to subsection (6)`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `s 204 a person or association`
         SHANT `s 204(5) deduct or retain an amount from the total amount of money, bets or stakes`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 204 a person or association` BECAUSE "s 204(5): an amount was deducted or retained otherwise than pursuant to subsection (6)"

-- src:4246 | (6) An association operating a pari-mutuel system of betting in accordance with this section in respect of a horse-race, or any other association or person acting on its behalf, may deduct and retain from the total amount of money that is bet through the agency of the pari-mutuel system, in respect of each individual pool of each race or each individual feature pool, a percentage not exceeding the percentage prescribed by the regulations plus any odd cents over any multiple of five cents in the amount calculated in accordance with the regulations to be payable in respect of each dollar bet.
@ref s 204(6) (src:4246-4246)
-- Fork F3: "any odd cents over any multiple of five cents in the amount calculated in accordance with the regulations to be payable in respect of each dollar bet" is read as an amount in dollars
-- that the caller supplies for the pool (the text leaves the calculation to the regulations).
GIVEN `the total amount of money that is bet, for the pool, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage prescribed by the regulations, as a decimal` IS A NUMBER
      `the odd cents over any multiple of five cents, for the pool, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount deducted and retained, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(6) the association may deduct and retain the amount` MEANS
    IF `the amount deducted and retained, in dollars` AT MOST (`the total amount of money that is bet, for the pool, in dollars` TIMES `the percentage prescribed by the regulations, as a decimal` PLUS `the odd cents over any multiple of five cents, for the pool, in dollars`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may deduct and retain ... a percentage not exceeding the percentage prescribed by the regulations plus any odd cents" (a grant; subsection (5) makes any other deduction a prohibited one)

-- src:4248 | (7) Where an officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food is not satisfied that the provisions of this section and the regulations are being carried out in good faith by any person or association in relation to a race meeting, he may, at any time, order any betting in relation to the race meeting to be stopped for any period that he considers proper.
@ref s 204(7) (src:4248-4248)
GIVEN `the officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food is not satisfied that the provisions of this section and the regulations are being carried out in good faith by the person or association in relation to the race meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(7) the officer may order any betting in relation to the race meeting to be stopped` MEANS
    IF `the officer appointed by the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food is not satisfied that the provisions of this section and the regulations are being carried out in good faith by the person or association in relation to the race meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an officer ... is not satisfied that the provisions of this section and the regulations are being carried out in good faith ... he may ... order any betting ... to be stopped"

-- src:4257 | (8.1) The Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food or a person designated by that Minister may, with respect to a horse-race conducted on a race-course situated outside Canada,
-- src:4258 | (a) certify as acceptable, for the purposes of this section, the governing body that regulates the race; and
-- src:4259 | (b) permit pari-mutuel betting in Canada on the race.
@ref s 204(8.1) (src:4257-4259)
GIVEN `the race is a horse-race conducted on a race-course situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acting is the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food or a person designated by that Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(8.1) the Minister or designated person may certify the governing body as acceptable and permit pari-mutuel betting in Canada on the race` MEANS
    IF `the race is a horse-race conducted on a race-course situated outside Canada` AND `the person acting is the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food or a person designated by that Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with respect to a horse-race conducted on a race-course situated outside Canada, (a) certify as acceptable ... (b) permit"

-- src:4270 | (9.1) For the purposes of this section, the Minister of Agriculture and Agri-Food may designate, with respect to any race-course, a zone that shall be deemed to be part of the race-course, if
-- src:4271 | (a) the zone is immediately adjacent to the race-course;
-- src:4272 | (b) the farthest point of that zone is not more than 900 metres from the nearest point on the race track of the race-course; and
-- src:4273 | (c) all real property situated in that zone is owned or leased by the person or association that owns or leases the race-course.
@ref s 204(9.1) (src:4270-4273)
GIVEN `the zone is immediately adjacent to the race-course` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distance of the farthest point of the zone from the nearest point on the race track of the race-course, in metres` IS A NUMBER
      `all real property situated in the zone is owned or leased by the person or association that owns or leases the race-course` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(9.1) the Minister may designate the zone, which is deemed to be part of the race-course` MEANS
    IF     `the zone is immediately adjacent to the race-course`
       AND `the distance of the farthest point of the zone from the nearest point on the race track of the race-course, in metres` AT MOST 900
       AND `all real property situated in the zone is owned or leased by the person or association that owns or leases the race-course`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may designate, with respect to any race-course, a zone that shall be deemed to be part of the race-course, if" (the three conditions; the function is named for a power, so a failed "if" is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE: fork F12)

-- src:4275 | (10) Every person who contravenes or fails to comply with any of the provisions of this section or of any regulations made under this section is guilty of
-- src:4276 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:4277 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 204(10) (src:4275-4277)
@ref s 204(10)(a) (src:4276-4276)
`s 204(10)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 204(10) (src:4275-4277)
GIVEN `the person contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of section 204 or of regulations made under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(10) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes or fails to comply with a provision of section 204 or of regulations made under it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who contravenes or fails to comply with any of the provisions of this section or of any regulations made under this section is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 204(10) (src:4275-4277)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 204(10) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 204(10) (src:4275-4277)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 204(10) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 204(10)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4279 | (11) For the purposes of this section, association means an association incorporated by or pursuant to an Act of Parliament or of the legislature of a province that owns or leases a race-course and conducts horse-races in the ordinary course of its business and, to the extent that the applicable legislation requires that the purposes of the association be expressly stated in its constating instrument, having as one of its purposes the conduct of horse-races.
@ref s 204(11) (src:4279-4279)
GIVEN `it is an association incorporated by or pursuant to an Act of Parliament or of the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it owns or leases a race-course` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it conducts horse-races in the ordinary course of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicable legislation requires that the purposes of the association be expressly stated in its constating instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of its purposes, so stated, is the conduct of horse-races` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(11) association` MEANS
    IF     `it is an association incorporated by or pursuant to an Act of Parliament or of the legislature of a province`
       AND `it owns or leases a race-course`
       AND `it conducts horse-races in the ordinary course of its business`
       AND ((NOT `the applicable legislation requires that the purposes of the association be expressly stated in its constating instrument`) OR `one of its purposes, so stated, is the conduct of horse-races`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "association means an association incorporated by or pursuant to an Act of Parliament or of the legislature of a province that owns or leases a race-course and conducts horse-races in the ordinary course of its business"
